            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.121,
            0.26,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.146,
            0.455,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Length of the land (l) = 12 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.17,
            0.421,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Width of land (w) = 10 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.198,
            0.716,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the whole land = l × w = 12 m × 10 m = 120 sq m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.226,
            0.806,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sidelength of each of the four square flower beds is (s) = 4 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.254,
            0.68,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of one flower bed "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "s \\times s = 4\\  m  \\times 4\\  m  = 16\\  sq \\  m"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.282,
            0.788,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, the area of the four flower beds = 4 × 16 sq m = 64 sq m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.307,
            0.884,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the area of the remaining part of the land is: area of the complete land minus the area of all four flower beds = 120 sq m – 64 sq m = 56 sq m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.366,
            0.353,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.398,
            0.884,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The area of a rectangular garden 25 m long is 300 sq m. What is the width of the garden?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.447,
            0.884,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What is the cost of tiling a rectangular plot of land 500 m long and 200 m wide at the rate of ` 8 per hundred sq m?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.495,
            0.886,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A rectangular coconut grove is 100 m long and 50 m wide. If each coconut tree requires 25 sq m, what is the maximum number of trees that can be planted in this grove?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
